From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joey Arhar <jarhar@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:45:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix use-after-free in direct pattern match cache

xsltTestCompMatchDirect reads the cached node-set for a pattern from the
transformation context's runtime extras before calling xmlXPathEval.
The evaluation can re-enter xsltTestCompMatchDirect for the same cache
slot, for example when a predicate references a global variable whose
lazily evaluated value runs xsl:number. The nested call can free and
replace the cached object, after which the outer call freed its stale
pointer again.

Re-read the cached object from the runtime extras after the evaluation
instead of using the value read before it.
---
 libxslt/pattern.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libxslt/pattern.c b/libxslt/pattern.c
index 581f17919fe3a..019a5cebbb31e 100644
--- a/libxslt/pattern.c
+++ b/libxslt/pattern.c
@@ -581,6 +581,15 @@ xsltTestCompMatchDirect(xsltTransformContextPtr ctxt, xsltCompMatchPtr comp,
 	    nocache = 1;
 
 	if (nocache == 0) {
+	    /*
+	     * xmlXPathEval can re-enter this function for the same cache
+	     * slot, e.g. through a lazily evaluated global variable whose
+	     * value runs xsl:number. The nested call may free or replace
+	     * the cached object, so re-read it instead of using the value
+	     * read before the evaluation.
+	     */
+	    list = (xmlXPathObjectPtr)
+		XSLT_RUNTIME_EXTRA_LST(ctxt, sel->lenExtra);
 	    if (list != NULL)
 		xmlXPathFreeObject(list);
 	    list = newlist;
--
